ize of the public key in bits.\0A * \5Cparam exponent The public exponent to use. For example, \5Cc 65537.\0A *                 This must be odd and greater than \5Cc 1.\0A *\0A * \5Creturn         \5Cc 0 on success.\0A * \5Creturn         An \5Cc MBEDTLS_ERR_RSA_XXX error code on failure.\0A */\0Aint mbedtls_rsa_gen_key(mbedtls_rsa_context *ctx,\0A                        int (*f_rng)(void *, unsigned char *, size_t),\0A                        void *p_rng,\0A                        unsigned int nbits, int exponent);\0A\0A/**\0A * \5Cbrief          This function checks if a context contains at least an RSA\0A *                 public key.\0A *\0A *                 If the function runs successfully, it is guaranteed that\0A *                 enough information is present to perform an RSA public key\0A *                 operation using mbedtls_rsa_public().\0A *\0A * \5Cparam ctx      The initialized RSA context to check.\0A *\0A * \5Creturn         \5Cc 0 on success.\0A * \5Creturn         An \5Cc MBEDTLS_ERR_RSA_XXX error code on failure.\0A *\0A */\0Aint mbedtls_rsa_check_pubkey(const mbedtls_rsa_context *ctx);\0A\0A/**\0A * \5Cbrief      This function checks if a context contains an RSA private key\0A *             and perform basic consistency checks.\0A *\0A * \5Cnote       The consistency checks performed by this function not only\0A *             ensure that mbedtls_rsa_private() can be called successfully\0A *             on the given context, but that the various parameters are\0A *             mutually consistent with high probability, in the sense that\0A *             mbedtls_rsa_public() and mbedtls_rsa_private() are inverses.\0A *\0A * \5Cwarning    This function should catch accidental misconfigurations\0A *             like swapping of parameters, but it cannot establish full\0A *             trust in neither the quality nor the consistency of the key\0A *             material that was used to setup the given RSA context:\0A *             <ul><li>Cons